# Build-context exclusions for frontend/Dockerfile.
#
# The single critical entry here is `.env*`: Vite inlines every VITE_* value
# it can read at build time straight into the shipped JS bundle. Without this
# file, a developer's local `.env.local` (API URLs, provider toggles, anything
# prefixed VITE_) silently leaks into the production image built on that host.
# The rest keeps the context small and the builds host-independent.

# Dependencies + build output — rebuilt inside the image; host copies are
# OS-specific (Windows-built native deps must never reach the Linux build).
node_modules
dist

# Env files — see the leak warning above. No exceptions: the image needs
# no env file at build time (CI builds prove it).
.env
.env.*

# E2E suite + test artefacts — irrelevant to the production bundle.
# `.playwright-auth.json` holds a live session cookie and must never be
# baked into an image.
e2e
playwright-report
test-results
coverage
.playwright-auth.json

# Local noise
*.log
